      "output": "# Roost — static review\n\nReview of the reports only. Nothing was run by me: \"not actually run.\"\n\n## Spec vs evidence\nThe spec follows the evidence and marks inference with `[o]/[i]`. Grounded: event kinds (text/multimodal/stop/handoff/tool-call/tool-result/chunk → say/plan/run/file/shot/fetch/ask/end), run statuses, `input_request`+timeout→ask cards, client replay with index+speed, AgentFlow lanes/edges, OpenAI-compatible model_client, WebSocket start/stop replaced by direct fetch, gallery→Library/Share/Import. Honestly inferred: handoff line, DM mirror, chip colours, lane-per-bot, and routines — evidence explicitly found **no** scheduling, so the spec marks routines as client-side added. Bots (wren/bram/ivy) and the garden session come from the brief, not the evidence app (AutoGen Studio); the spec says so. Consistent.\n\n## Acceptance checks — numbering mismatch (flag)\nThe **spec declares 31 numbered tests and 11 planted failures** (§9, §10). The **test report instead reports 64 tests and 20 planted**, grouped only by module (core 8, shell 6, vfs 8, chat 6, bots 8, computer 6, skills 6, replay 10, agent 6). It gives **no per-number results** for spec 1–31, so I cannot confirm each numbered check by its number — not shown. The documents share neither count nor IDs.\n\nPassing: report states **64 of 64 ok:true**, empty details, 0 page errors, not blank. Failing by number: **none listed**, none mappable to spec 1–31.\n\nPlanted caught: report states **20 of 20 rejected**. The spec's named plants P1–P11 (e.g. P5 speed=1 not 2, P7 code 1 not 127, P9 avatar hex, P11 throw uncaught) are **not individually confirmed by id**; only a total of 20 is given.\n\n## Fixes\nReport: **no fixes** — no failing tests, no page errors, no edits to roost.html.\n\n## Spec coverage gaps (no shown check maps to)\nNo listed test for: the ≥40 commands/palette (§3), theme tokens/layout sizes (§5), approval allow/deny (§7), routine *firing* in live mode, model non-2xx and >20-call limits, Connectors \"blocked in preview\", Share/Import JSON and id-clash suffixing, DM unread reset, handoff gap marker. The report's extra modular tests may cover some, but their contents are not shown.\n\n## Overall\nSpec is evidence-faithful and marks inference. The PASS, 64/64 and 20/20 are the report's claims — not actually run by me, and not reconcilable number-for-number with the spec's 31/11.\n",
